{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is running a cobbler-scaffold stitch task (#5387) that requires implementing srd054-tr requirements R4.1, R4.2, and R4.3 for the `cmd/tr` (translate/delete characters) utility. Specifically:\n   - **R4.1**: Must exit 0 when translation or deletion completes successfully.\n   - **R4.2**: Must exit 1 on usage errors (missing SET, invalid class, conflicting flags).\n   - **R4.3**: Differential tests must compare stdout output and exit codes between the Go binary and the reference binary (gtr) via pkg/testutils. Tests must cover: basic translation, -d delete, -s squeeze, -c complement, -ds combined, character ranges, POSIX classes, case conversion, octal escapes, and error cases.\n   \n   Files to modify: `cmd/tr/main.go` and `cmd/tr/tr_test.go`. The task follows strict execution constitution rules (no git commands, no scope creep, all acceptance criteria must pass).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern: Go binary vs GNU reference binary (gtr) using `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests`\n   - SIGPIPE handler via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - DiffTest struct with Name, Args, Stdin, ExitCode, Normalize, and Env fields\n   - Exit code conventions: 0 for success, 1 for usage errors\n   - Character class/range/escape/equivalence class expansion in SET specifications\n   - LC_ALL=C environment for all tests\n   - NormalizeFunc for stderr comparison (binary name normalization, usage hint stripping)\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd054-tr.yaml**\n     - Source of truth for R4.1-R4.3 requirements\n     - R4.1: exit 0 on success; R4.2: exit 1 on usage errors; R4.3: comprehensive differential tests\n     - Non-goals: no multibyte support, no file arguments\n   \n   - **cmd/tr/main.go** (465 lines, existing implementation)\n     - Already implements R1.1-R1.4, R2.1-R2.4, R3.1-R3.3 from prior tasks\n     - `main()` calls `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`, `parseArgs()`, `run()`, exits 1 on error\n     - Key functions: `parseArgs`, `parseShortFlags`, `validateOperands`, `run`, `expandSet`, `process`, `buildTable`, `complementSet`, `memberSet`\n     - Exit behavior: implicit exit 0 on success, explicit `os.Exit(1)` on parseArgs or run error\n     - `validateOperands` handles: missing operand, extra operand with -d, missing operand after first SET\n     - Current main function:\n       ```go\n       func main() {\n           sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n           cfg, err := parseArgs(os.Args[1:])\n           if err != nil {\n               fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"tr: %s\\n\", err)\n               os.Exit(1)\n           }\n           if err := run(cfg); err != nil {\n               fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"tr: %s\\n\", err)\n               os.Exit(1)\n           }\n       }\n       ```\n   \n   - **cmd/tr/tr_test.go** (94 lines, existing tests)\n     - Uses `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` and `exec.LookPath(\"gtr\")`\n     - Has normalizers: `normalizeBinaryName` and `normalizeUsageHints`\n     - errNorm used for error cases: `[]testutils.NormalizeFunc{normalizeBinaryName, normalizeUsageHints}`\n     - Already has tests for: basic translate, case conversion, delete, squeeze, complement, character classes, octal escapes, equivalence classes, error cases (empty set2, missing operand, missing set2)\n     - Tests with ExitCode: 1 exist for r3_empty_set2, r3_missing_operand, r3_missing_set2, r3_equiv_set2_translate_err\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet - work had not begun implementation phase.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Read all three required files to understand existing implementation and test coverage\n   - Was in the analysis phase determining what changes are needed for R4.1-R4.3\n   - R4.1 (exit 0 on success) appears already implemented via Go's default exit behavior\n   - R4.2 (exit 1 on errors) appears largely implemented but may need additional validation for \"conflicting flags\" or \"invalid class\" error paths\n   - R4.3 (comprehensive tests) requires adding differential test cases that explicitly verify exit codes for success and error cases, and ensure all listed categories have coverage\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - The initial message is the full stitch task prompt with all project context, SRDs, architecture, requirements, and instructions for task #5387: implementing srd054-tr R4.1-R4.3.\n   - \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - User requested a summary of the conversation, explicitly forbidding tool use.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Implement any missing exit code handling in `cmd/tr/main.go` for R4.1 and R4.2\n   - Add comprehensive differential test cases to `cmd/tr/tr_test.go` for R4.3 covering all required categories with explicit exit code verification\n   - Run `go build ./cmd/tr/` to verify compilation\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/tr/ -count=1` to verify tests pass\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading the three required files (srd054-tr.yaml, cmd/tr/main.go, cmd/tr/tr_test.go) and was about to plan the implementation approach. No code changes have been made yet. The analysis reveals:\n   - R4.1 and R4.2 are mostly already satisfied by the existing `main()` function's error handling\n   - R4.3 requires adding test cases that explicitly set `ExitCode: 0` for success cases (to verify exit code matching) and additional error-case tests with `ExitCode: 1` for invalid classes, conflicting flags, etc.\n   - The existing test file has ~50 test cases but may need additional ones specifically for: verifying exit 0 on success paths, invalid character class errors, and potentially other usage error scenarios\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Implement the R4.1-R4.3 requirements by:\n   1. Reviewing